{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":81065,"num_turns":3,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"ec2c551e-f72e-5ba9-9431-67865e1857e0","total_cost_usd":0.692624,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13632,"cache_read_input_tokens":9432,"output_tokens":8131,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13632,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3989,"cache_read_input_tokens":9432,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4200,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4200},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":3882,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.003962,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":8131,"cacheReadInputTokens":9432,"cacheCreationInputTokens":13632,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.688662,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\":\"actor:dependence-free-batch-h1-reviewer-fable-36\",\"reviews\":[{\"case_id\":\"case:95b0d17896ce31b504a0\",\"verdict\":\"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\",\"bounded_statement\":null,\"root_cause\":null,\"issue_class\":null,\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The data contain repeated within-bee measurements (305 nest departures across 23 bees), which are the only potential source of repeated independent-unit entries; they appear as per-bee summary counts, not as separate rows.\",\"observed_value\":{\"total_departures\":305,\"n_bees\":23},\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":8,\"end_line\":13,\"quoted_text\":\"For every bee an observer scored a run of departures from the nest entrance and\\nnoted, for each departure, whether the bee circled clockwise or counterclockwise\\nbefore flying off. Those repeated within-bee departures appear in the file only\\nas two summary counts; the analysis reduces them to a single majority-direction\\ncall for that bee before anything is tested, so no individual departure is ever\\ntreated as its own observation.\"},{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":2,\"quoted_text\":\"bee_id,meadow_patch,forewing_length_mm,departures_scored,clockwise_departures\\nB01,M01,9.4,13,9\"}]},{\"description\":\"The description names bee_id as the independent-unit column and states one line per bee, defining the unit against which repeated-entry would have to be judged.\",\"observed_value\":\"bee_id; one row per bee\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":15,\"end_line\":17,\"quoted_text\":\"One row is: one individual mason bee, summarised over all of the nest departures scored for her at her own meadow patch\\nIndependent unit column: bee_id\\nOne trial is: one row\"}]},{\"description\":\"The report's selected result is an exact binomial test whose count and denominator are bee-level (17 of 23), the quantity that must be checked against the independent-unit definition.\",\"observed_value\":{\"successes\":17,\"n\":23,\"p_value\":0.0347},\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":22,\"end_line\":22,\"quoted_text\":\"[selected-result] Exact two-sided binomial test on one majority-direction call per bee: 17/23 bees (0.739) circled clockwise more often than counterclockwise, p = 0.0347; the 50:50 no-bias null is rejected at alpha = 0.05.\"}]}],\"counterevidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The workflow collapses each bee's repeated departures to a single majority-direction call and passes only the per-bee tally to the test, so binomtest receives exactly one entry per independent unit (n = 23 bees, not 305 departures).\",\"observed_value\":\"binomtest(n_clockwise, n_bees, 0.5) with n_bees = 23\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":45,\"end_line\":50,\"quoted_text\":\"    calls = [majority_call(row) for row in rows]\\n    n_bees = len(calls)\\n    n_clockwise = calls.count(\\\"clockwise\\\")\\n    departures = sum(int(row[\\\"departures_scored\\\"]) for row in rows)\\n\\n    test = binomtest(n_clockwise, n_bees, NULL_SHARE, alternative=\\\"two-sided\\\")\"},{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":29,\"end_line\":37,\"quoted_text\":\"def majority_call(row: dict[str, str]) -> str:\\n    scored = int(row[\\\"departures_scored\\\"])\\n    clockwise = int(row[\\\"clockwise_departures\\\"])\\n    counterclockwise = scored - clockwise\\n    if counterclockwise < 0:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"impossible counts for bee \\\" + row[\\\"bee_id\\\"])\\n    if clockwise == counterclockwise:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"tied bee has no majority: \\\" + row[\\\"bee_id\\\"])\\n    return \\\"clockwise\\\" if clockwise > counterclockwise else \\\"counterclockwise\\\"\"}]},{\"description\":\"The workflow explicitly enforces that bee_id identifies exactly one row, ruling out duplicated independent-unit rows entering the procedure.\",\"observed_value\":\"uniqueness check on bee_id raises on duplicates\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":41,\"end_line\":43,\"quoted_text\":\"    rows = read_rows(INPUT_PATH)\\n    if len({row[\\\"bee_id\\\"] for row in rows}) != len(rows):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"bee_id must identify exactly one row\\\")\"}]},{\"description\":\"Independent recomputation from the raw CSV confirms the reported bee-level statistics: 17 of 23 bees have a clockwise majority (departures_scored is always odd, so no ties), total departures sum to 305, and the exact two-sided binomial p-value is 2 * 145499/8388608 ~= 0.0347, matching the report; each meadow_patch (M01-M23) holds exactly one bee, so patches introduce no cross-row dependence.\",\"observed_value\":{\"recomputed_clockwise_majority\":17,\"recomputed_n\":23,\"recomputed_total_departures\":305,\"recomputed_p_value\":0.0347},\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":2,\"end_line\":24,\"quoted_text\":\"B01,M01,9.4,13,9\\nB02,M02,8.9,11,4\\nB03,M03,9.8,15,10\\nB04,M04,9.1,9,6\\nB05,M05,10.2,17,12\\nB06,M06,8.6,11,7\\nB07,M07,9.5,13,5\\nB08,M08,9.9,15,9\\nB09,M09,8.8,9,7\\nB10,M10,10.0,19,11\\nB11,M11,9.3,11,3\\nB12,M12,9.6,13,8\\nB13,M13,8.5,9,5\\nB14,M14,10.4,17,10\\nB15,M15,9.2,15,6\\nB16,M16,9.7,11,8\\nB17,M17,8.7,13,7\\nB18,M18,10.1,9,4\\nB19,M19,9.0,15,11\\nB20,M20,9.4,11,6\\nB21,M21,10.3,19,13\\nB22,M22,8.4,13,6\\nB23,M23,9.9,17,9\"},{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":18,\"end_line\":20,\"quoted_text\":\"- Clockwise-majority bees: 17 of 23 (0.739)\\n- Counterclockwise-majority bees: 6\\n- Exact two-sided p-value: 0.0347\"}]},{\"description\":\"The report's design statement accurately describes the executed workflow: departures are not analysed individually and the analysed sample is one call per bee, consistent with the code path.\",\"observed_value\":\"report design text matches code behaviour\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":5,\"end_line\":9,\"quoted_text\":\"Each of the 23 bees in `data/input.csv` occupied its own meadow patch and\\ncontributes exactly one row. The 305 scored departures are not analysed\\nindividually: within a bee the departures are collapsed to a single majority\\ncall (clockwise or counterclockwise), so the analysed sample is one call per\\nbee.\"}]}],\"falsification_attempt\":\"I tried to demonstrate the issue by searching for any route through which more than one entry per bee reaches the binomial test: (1) checked whether the test statistic could be departure-level, but the code passes calls.count('clockwise') out of len(calls) where calls has exactly one element per CSV row, and the departure sum is computed only for narrative text, never passed to binomtest; (2) checked for duplicate bee_id rows in data/input.csv, finding 23 distinct IDs B01-B23 across 23 data rows, and the code additionally raises on duplicates; (3) checked whether the reported p = 0.0347 could only arise from a departure-level test, but recomputing by hand gives exactly 17 clockwise-majority bees and a two-sided exact p of 2 * 145499/8388608 ~= 0.0347 for 17/23 at p0 = 0.5, so the reported result is the bee-level test (a departure-level pooled test would use 305 trials, which nothing in the code constructs); (4) checked meadow_patch for shared-unit clustering, but each patch value appears once, matching the stated one-bee-per-patch design. Every attempt failed, so the issue is not demonstrated.\",\"cross_case_evidence_used\":false,\"unresolved_material_questions\":[],\"self_reported_confidence\":\"high\"}]}","structured_output":{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:dependence-free-batch-h1-reviewer-fable-36","reviews":[{"case_id":"case:95b0d17896ce31b504a0","verdict":"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope","bounded_statement":null,"root_cause":null,"issue_class":null,"evidence_atoms":[{"description":"The data contain repeated within-bee measurements (305 nest departures across 23 bees), which are the only potential source of repeated independent-unit entries; they appear as per-bee summary counts, not as separate rows.","observed_value":{"total_departures":305,"n_bees":23},"source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":8,"end_line":13,"quoted_text":"For every bee an observer scored a run of departures from the nest entrance and\nnoted, for each departure, whether the bee circled clockwise or counterclockwise\nbefore flying off. Those repeated within-bee departures appear in the file only\nas two summary counts; the analysis reduces them to a single majority-direction\ncall for that bee before anything is tested, so no individual departure is ever\ntreated as its own observation."},{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":1,"end_line":2,"quoted_text":"bee_id,meadow_patch,forewing_length_mm,departures_scored,clockwise_departures\nB01,M01,9.4,13,9"}]},{"description":"The description names bee_id as the independent-unit column and states one line per bee, defining the unit against which repeated-entry would have to be judged.","observed_value":"bee_id; one row per bee","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":15,"end_line":17,"quoted_text":"One row is: one individual mason bee, summarised over all of the nest departures scored for her at her own meadow patch\nIndependent unit column: bee_id\nOne trial is: one row"}]},{"description":"The report's selected result is an exact binomial test whose count and denominator are bee-level (17 of 23), the quantity that must be checked against the independent-unit definition.","observed_value":{"successes":17,"n":23,"p_value":0.0347},"source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":22,"end_line":22,"quoted_text":"[selected-result] Exact two-sided binomial test on one majority-direction call per bee: 17/23 bees (0.739) circled clockwise more often than counterclockwise, p = 0.0347; the 50:50 no-bias null is rejected at alpha = 0.05."}]}],"counterevidence_atoms":[{"description":"The workflow collapses each bee's repeated departures to a single majority-direction call and passes only the per-bee tally to the test, so binomtest receives exactly one entry per independent unit (n = 23 bees, not 305 departures).","observed_value":"binomtest(n_clockwise, n_bees, 0.5) with n_bees = 23","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":45,"end_line":50,"quoted_text":"    calls = [majority_call(row) for row in rows]\n    n_bees = len(calls)\n    n_clockwise = calls.count(\"clockwise\")\n    departures = sum(int(row[\"departures_scored\"]) for row in rows)\n\n    test = binomtest(n_clockwise, n_bees, NULL_SHARE, alternative=\"two-sided\")"},{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":29,"end_line":37,"quoted_text":"def majority_call(row: dict[str, str]) -> str:\n    scored = int(row[\"departures_scored\"])\n    clockwise = int(row[\"clockwise_departures\"])\n    counterclockwise = scored - clockwise\n    if counterclockwise < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"impossible counts for bee \" + row[\"bee_id\"])\n    if clockwise == counterclockwise:\n        raise ValueError(\"tied bee has no majority: \" + row[\"bee_id\"])\n    return \"clockwise\" if clockwise > counterclockwise else \"counterclockwise\""}]},{"description":"The workflow explicitly enforces that bee_id identifies exactly one row, ruling out duplicated independent-unit rows entering the procedure.","observed_value":"uniqueness check on bee_id raises on duplicates","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":41,"end_line":43,"quoted_text":"    rows = read_rows(INPUT_PATH)\n    if len({row[\"bee_id\"] for row in rows}) != len(rows):\n        raise ValueError(\"bee_id must identify exactly one row\")"}]},{"description":"Independent recomputation from the raw CSV confirms the reported bee-level statistics: 17 of 23 bees have a clockwise majority (departures_scored is always odd, so no ties), total departures sum to 305, and the exact two-sided binomial p-value is 2 * 145499/8388608 ~= 0.0347, matching the report; each meadow_patch (M01-M23) holds exactly one bee, so patches introduce no cross-row dependence.","observed_value":{"recomputed_clockwise_majority":17,"recomputed_n":23,"recomputed_total_departures":305,"recomputed_p_value":0.0347},"source_spans":[{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":2,"end_line":24,"quoted_text":"B01,M01,9.4,13,9\nB02,M02,8.9,11,4\nB03,M03,9.8,15,10\nB04,M04,9.1,9,6\nB05,M05,10.2,17,12\nB06,M06,8.6,11,7\nB07,M07,9.5,13,5\nB08,M08,9.9,15,9\nB09,M09,8.8,9,7\nB10,M10,10.0,19,11\nB11,M11,9.3,11,3\nB12,M12,9.6,13,8\nB13,M13,8.5,9,5\nB14,M14,10.4,17,10\nB15,M15,9.2,15,6\nB16,M16,9.7,11,8\nB17,M17,8.7,13,7\nB18,M18,10.1,9,4\nB19,M19,9.0,15,11\nB20,M20,9.4,11,6\nB21,M21,10.3,19,13\nB22,M22,8.4,13,6\nB23,M23,9.9,17,9"},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":18,"end_line":20,"quoted_text":"- Clockwise-majority bees: 17 of 23 (0.739)\n- Counterclockwise-majority bees: 6\n- Exact two-sided p-value: 0.0347"}]},{"description":"The report's design statement accurately describes the executed workflow: departures are not analysed individually and the analysed sample is one call per bee, consistent with the code path.","observed_value":"report design text matches code behaviour","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":5,"end_line":9,"quoted_text":"Each of the 23 bees in `data/input.csv` occupied its own meadow patch and\ncontributes exactly one row. The 305 scored departures are not analysed\nindividually: within a bee the departures are collapsed to a single majority\ncall (clockwise or counterclockwise), so the analysed sample is one call per\nbee."}]}],"falsification_attempt":"I tried to demonstrate the issue by searching for any route through which more than one entry per bee reaches the binomial test: (1) checked whether the test statistic could be departure-level, but the code passes calls.count('clockwise') out of len(calls) where calls has exactly one element per CSV row, and the departure sum is computed only for narrative text, never passed to binomtest; (2) checked for duplicate bee_id rows in data/input.csv, finding 23 distinct IDs B01-B23 across 23 data rows, and the code additionally raises on duplicates; (3) checked whether the reported p = 0.0347 could only arise from a departure-level test, but recomputing by hand gives exactly 17 clockwise-majority bees and a two-sided exact p of 2 * 145499/8388608 ~= 0.0347 for 17/23 at p0 = 0.5, so the reported result is the bee-level test (a departure-level pooled test would use 305 trials, which nothing in the code constructs); (4) checked meadow_patch for shared-unit clustering, but each patch value appears once, matching the stated one-bee-per-patch design. Every attempt failed, so the issue is not demonstrated.","cross_case_evidence_used":false,"unresolved_material_questions":[],"self_reported_confidence":"high"}]},"ttft_ms":35284,"ttft_stream_ms":1768,"time_to_request_ms":11,"type":"result","duration_ms":80101,"uuid":"f2254797-391d-40f3-a43e-0eb7792f3076"}
